{"path":"/work/workspace/deliverable/child_support.json","content":"{
  "husband_gross_used": 189000,
  "wife_gross_used": 96000,
  "combined_monthly_net": 18525.00,
  "basic_obligation": 3050,
  "husband_share_monthly": 2022.63,
  "notes": "Guideline income includes expected bonuses evidenced by employer documents (Col. Rev. Stat. 14-10-115): Husband's true gross = 168,000 salary + 45,000 HR-letter target bonus = 213,000 (possibly 50,400 actual at his 112%-of-plan pace). Worksheet adjustment: maintenance paid between the parties is subtracted from payor / added to recipient before computing support -> Husband 213,000 - 24,000 (2,000/mo maintenance) = 189,000 (used above); Wife 72,000 + 24,000 = 96,000. Nets (gross x 0.78 / 12): H 189,000 x 0.78 / 12 = 12,285.00; W 96,000 x 0.78 / 12 = 6,240.00; combined 18,525.00 -> bracket '15,000 < x <= 20,000' -> basic obligation 3,050 (two children). Husband share = 3,050 x 12,285/18,525 = 3,050 x 0.66316 = 2,022.63/mo. The proposal's salary-only basis (144,000 adj / 96,000; nets 9,360 + 6,240 = 15,600, same 3,050 bracket) yields only 3,050 x 0.60 = 1,830.00 -> underpayment 192.63/mo, 2,311.58/yr while children are minors. If maintenance were instead NOT counted in the worksheet the result would be 2,279.47/mo (13,845/18,525); the guidelines as written require the adjustment. No shared-parenting adjustment: Husband has ~30% overnights, below the 35% threshold; Wife is the residential parent (>= 65%). Duration to majority is not specified in the library (children 9 and 12) - unverified; ask (QUESTIONS.md)."
}
"}

